cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the Version 2 Zenodo reproducibility record."
title: "Jolo Island Surface Heat GeoAI: Reproducibility Package"
type: dataset

authors:
  - family-names: "Adju"
    given-names: "Fadzlur-Nijar A."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-1865-7596"
    affiliation: "College of Computing Studies, Mindanao State University–Sulu, Philippines"

version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-09"

abstract: >-
  Version 2.0.0 provides the complete reproducibility archive for a matched
  geographic validation study of prediction and model-attribution transfer
  in environmental GeoAI using land-surface temperature across Jolo Island,
  Philippines. The archive contains the frozen Version 1 modelling baseline
  together with Version 2 spatial transfer, SHAP attribution-stability,
  municipality-held-out, environmental-support, block-origin,
  cross-algorithm, dominant-predictor ablation, seasonal robustness,
  seed-sensitivity, and residual spatial-diagnostic outputs.

keywords:
  - "environmental GeoAI"
  - "land surface temperature"
  - "geographic transferability"
  - "prediction transfer"
  - "model attribution"
  - "SHAP"
  - "spatial cross-validation"
  - "explainable machine learning"
  - "Landsat"
  - "Jolo Island"
  - "Philippines"

